<Shell title="Sources & credits" description="How Return to Morroc: Refuge Fieldnotes credits public source guides and separates source material from editorial updates.">
  <div class="about-page"><span class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE FIELDNOTES</span><h1>Good knowledge deserves<br />a clear trail home.</h1><div class="prose">
    <p>Return to Morroc: Refuge Fieldnotes is an independent personal guide library. It brings publicly available guide material into a common reading format. It is not the server's official website.</p>
    <h2>Credit stays with the creators</h2><p>Every guide lists its source links and original authors. The first community reference is <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/1KVRrnLTCRxi_ou5hQrZS7mDr-W2aBcUD2uZKclWuyyo/edit">The New Orphan’s Guide To Morroc</a>, by Gryph, with the introduction and framework by Agent Q. Its full contributor acknowledgements remain in the original.</p>
    <h2>Dates mean different things</h2><p>An editorial update records a change to this page. Source review means the cited material was checked. In-game verification is recorded separately and is not implied by either date.</p>
    <h2>Artwork and type</h2><p>The scenic illustrations and class portraits are sourced from the <a href="https://rtmrefuge.pages.dev/">Refuge website</a>, which states its site content is free to copy. Third-party artwork remains the property of its respective owners. The New Player Guide includes eight original document images, with source attribution beside the instructions.</p><p>Amarante and Atkinson Hyperlegible are distributed under the SIL Open Font License. Their license files are included alongside the local fonts. The Refuge mark is a local copy of the <a href="https://rtm-database.pages.dev/">database website's header image</a>; the Fieldnotes wordmark and interface are created for this library.</p>
    <p>Orphan skill icons come from the <a href="https://rtm-database.pages.dev/skills.html">Refuge database</a>. Orphanage NPC sprites were matched against owner-provided screenshots using <a href="https://rune-nifelheim.com/npc/">Rune Nifelheim</a> and <a href="https://ratemyragnarok.com/npcs/">Rate My Ragnarok</a>, and rendered with <a href="https://github.com/adsonpleal/ragassets">RagAssets</a>. Ragnarok Online artwork belongs to Gravity and its respective creators.</p>
    <h2>A small beginning</h2><p>The New Player Guide, Job Class Tree, and Thief class guide are available. Other class guides, Leveling Spots, Dungeons, Distortions, and quest guides are works in progress.</p>
  </div><Footer /></div>
</Shell>
